<title>ZIMBABWE: Bindura yr shr slides, cuts div.</title>
<headline>Bindura yr shr slides, cuts div.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(all figures in Z$ million unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		   130.1     vs    219.5</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		    55.0     vs    100.0</p>
<p>    After-tax profit	 151.95     vs    256.41</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    154.89     vs    268.40</p>
<p>    Tax			    2.94     vs    11.99</p>
<p>    Interest paid	     15.50     vs    0.69</p>
<p>    Turnover		   978.93     vs    883.26</p>
<p>Div payable April 25</p>
<p>on register March 28</p>
<p>Full name: Bindura Nickel Corporation Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it generally expected profits for 1997 to exceed those of the year under review. But it said maintaining an adequate profit would be difficult in an economic environment in which the Zimbabwean exchange rate was not depreciating as fast as general inflation.</p>
<p>-- Harare newsroom +263-4 72 52 28/9</p>
</text>
